# Nested arrays (A7, B14): an enclosed item has type Box a, and a nested
# array prints as APL2's DISPLAY shows it: a frame per array, an arrow
# along the top (and one down the left per leading axis), and a mark at
# the bottom: ~ for numbers, nothing for characters, a membership sign
# for an array holding boxes. A box of a simple scalar is framed too.
== SOURCE
"ab" "cde"
t_ally "ab" "cde"
d_isclose 2 s_elect "ab" "cde"
e_nclose "abc"
e_nclose 5
(e_nclose 1) c_at e_nclose 2 3
2 2 r_eshape "a" "bb" "ccc" "d"
e_nclose "ab" "cd"
== TYPE
Box Char
Int
Char
Box Char
Box Int
Box Int
Box Char
Box (Box Char)
